 },\r\n  \"observed\": {\r\n    \"effort\": \"unknown\",\r\n    \"source\": \"cli_terminal_model_usage\",\r\n    \"model\": \"claude-opus-5-5\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"review\": {\r\n    \"summary\": \"I reviewed only the supplied test, disposition and deadline contract. Overall the test design holds up: each iteration gets its own browser context, requests to other origins are blocked, and each engine sends 8 POSTs (two per iteration). The closed-behavior branches are backed by specific text, readonly and URL checks. One check can give a false pass: in the redirect branch, the expired-success step would pass even if the success receipt were lost or an error page rendered. Two recorded claims (noResubmit, noMailSent) go further than what is actually tested. The bogus-query check doesn't confirm that the retry view is absent, and cleanup relies on unconfirmed cascade deletes. There are no blockers. None of this amounts to full WP acceptance: human assistive-technology checks and regression on other entry points are still pending. The disposition's claim that running the engines in separate processes isolates the rate limit depends on the external runner and on whether the rate limiter is per-process, and neither was supplied.\",\r\n    \"findings\": [\r\n      {\r\n        \"severity\": \"MAJOR\",\r\n        \"file\": \"browser-deadline.cjs\",\r\n        \"area\": \"expired-success, the behavior==='redirect' else branch, and the page.reload() just before it\",\r\n        \"issue\": \"In the redirect branch, the expired-success check can pass even when the product is broken. The browser is already at the thank-you path after the successful submit. Even if it weren't, the normal deadline redirect would send it there. So the pathname assertion would pass whether or not the deadline logic works. The other checks are 'no closed heading' and 'no form/input/submit', and a thank-you page usually has none of those anyway. The reload response status is never checked, and no receipt or verification text is checked.\",\r\n        \"evidence\": \"`await page.reload();` ignores the response. The branch asserts only `pathname === '/lp/'+key+'/thank-you'`, a closed-heading count of 0, and a form/input count of 0. Then `report.checks` records `verifiedSuccess:'configured-target-remains-viewable'`.\",\r\n        \"impact\": \"Several product failures would still pass and be recorded as verified: a 404 or 500 page at the thank-you path, a thank-you page that drops the submitted=verification_required receipt, or a normal expiry redirect that strips the query. That makes the redirect-behavior success claim a false positive.\",\r\n        \"recommended_fix\": \"Capture `const res = await page.reload()` and assert `res.status() === 200`. Assert that the query still contains `submitted=verification_required`. Wait for the specific verification receipt text (the same 請到 Email 開啟確認連結… string, or whatever text the thank-you step renders). Also assert the pathname right after the successful submit, before calling close(), so the redirect-branch assertion actually separates 'receipt kept' from 'redirected by expiry'.\",\r\n        \"required_test\": \"Break things on purpose and confirm the redirect branch fails: (a) make the thank-you step throw or return 404 when expired; (b) drop the receipt query parameter on expiry. Re-run on both engines.\",\r\n        \"confidence\": 0.8\r\n      },\r\n      {\r\n        \"severity\": \"MINOR\",\r\n        \"file\": \"browser-deadline.cjs\",\r\n        \"area\": \"report.checks push: noResubmit:true; the formSubmission count asserted after the reload\",\r\n        \"issue\": \"The `noResubmit` claim is never actually tested. After expiry the test only checks that no form is rendered and reloads a page loaded by GET (the server redirects after each POST), and a GET reload can never create a submission. Nothing POSTs to the expired source or to the expired-but-viewable redirect target, so the isFunnelDeadlineExpired write block is never tested.\",\r\n        \"evidence\": \"The only POSTs are the invalid submit and the success submit, both sent while the deadline is open. The count of 1 is checked after `page.reload()` of a GET URL. The contract comment says 'Expiry also blocks form and checkout writes on an otherwise viewable redirect target'.\",\r\n        \"impact\": \"The report says resubmission after expiry is blocked when only the absence of rendered controls was observed. If the server-side expiry write check regressed, this test would not notice.\",\r\n        \"recommended_fix\": \"Either rename or narrow the flag (e.g., `noSubmitControls`), or add one direct native POST per engine against an expired page, closed and redirect-target, using `context.request` or a saved form. The per-engine budget has room: 9–10 of the 10/min limit. Assert the response is rejected and the formSubmission count does not change.\",\r\n        \"required_test\": \"While expired, POST one valid synthetic registration to the source route and confirm it is rejected with no new formSubmission row. Repeat for the redirect target when behavior is redirect, keeping each engine at or under 10 POSTs.\",\r\n        \"confidence\": 0.75\r\n      },\r\n      {\r\n        \"severity\": \"MINOR\",\r\n        \"file\": \"browser-deadline.cjs\",\r\n        \"area\": \"normal-expiry step (?registrationRetry=bogus)\",\r\n        \"issue\": \"The comment says an unknown query 'must not expose a retry view', but the closed branch only waits for the generic closed text. It never asserts that the retry-view messages are absent, and never checks the form/input count. In the redirect branch only the pathname is checked.\",\r\n        \"evidence\": \"In the closed branch the only assertion is `await page.getByText('目前不再接受新的瀏覽或送出資料。').waitFor()`. There are no count-0 checks for '先前送出未完成…', '無法確認先前的送出結果…' or the input/form selector.\",\r\n        \"impact\": \"If the product treated an unknown retry code as a retry view, for example by rendering the cross-path 'cannot confirm' message next to the closed copy, the test would still pass while reporting `normalDeadlinePreserved:true`.\",\r\n        \"recommended_fix\": \"In both branches, assert that both retry-view strings have a count of 0, that `input,form,button[type=submit],main button` has a count of 0, and that the response status is 200 (or a redirect followed by a 200 in the redirect branch).\",\r\n        \"required_test\": \"Temporarily make the retry view render for any registrationRetry value and confirm the normal-expiry step fails.\",\r\n        \"confidence\": 0.65\r\n      },\r\n      {\r\n        \"severity\": \"MINOR\",\r\n        \"file\": \"browser-deadline.cjs\",\r\n        \"area\": \"finally cleanup block\",\r\n        \"issue\": \"Cleanup deletes some tables explicitly but relies on unconfirmed cascade deletes from vendor for formSubmission (4 rows per engine with real emails), registrationForm, salesProject, emailDelivery and any verification-token rows. Nothing checks afterwards that no rows remain. `report.cleanup=true` only means nothing threw.\",\r\n        \"evidence\": \"The explicit deletes cover registrationFormRetryDraft, funnelSubmission, landingPage(Version) and vendor. formSubmission, registrationForm, salesProject and emailDelivery are never deleted by name. The landingPage/version steps are ordered carefully, which suggests some relations are Restrict rather than Cascade.\",\r\n        \"impact\": \"If a relation is Restrict, vendor.delete fails and synthetic rows stay behind (reported, but not cleaned). If a table has no vendor relation, rows stay behind silently, and repeated runs build up synthetic submissions and deliveries in the shared local database.\",\r\n        \"recommended_fix\": \"Explicitly delete formSubmission, emailDelivery or verification rows, registrationForm and salesProject for this vendor/form before deleting the vendor. Then check that zero rows remain for vendor.id, form.id and `key`, and set `report.cleanup` only after that check passes.\",\r\n        \"required_test\": \"Run one engine, then query every table touched by the submit path for the vendor id, form id and key slug and confirm the counts are zero. Also check cleanup after a failure injected at the success-before-expiry stage.\",\r\n        \"confidence\": 0.6\r\n      },\r\n      {\r\n        \"severity\": \"NIT\",\r\n        \"file\": \"browser-deadline.cjs\",\r\n        \"area\": \"emailDelivery count assertion, report noMailSent:true\",\r\n        \"issue\": \"`noMailSent` is a single check that no delivery has status 'sent' at that moment. If the local environment has no mail provider, or delivery runs asynchronously, the check is trivially true. If a real provider is configured, the mail has already gone out before the check runs.\",\r\n        \"evidence\": \"`db.emailDelivery.count({where:{vendorId:vendor.id,status:'sent'}}) === 0` runs right after the pages load, with no check of the provider configuration or of queued, failed or processing rows.\",\r\n        \"impact\": \"The flag suggests a stronger guarantee than the check provides. The real protection is the reserved example.test domain.\",\r\n        \"recommended_fix\": \"Rename it to something like `noSentDeliveryObserved`. Otherwise, assert at startup that the mail transport is a local, disabled or capture transport, and count all delivery statuses.\",\r\n        \"required_test\": \"Assert the configured mail transport at startup and record it in the report.\",\r\n        \"confidence\": 0.5\r\n      }\r\n    ]\r\n  },\r\n  \"normalized_status\": \"REVIEW_COMPLETED\",\r\n  \"completed\": false,\r\n  \"finalModel\": \"claude-opus-5-5\",\r\n  \"requested\": {\r\n    \"model_key\": \"opus\",\r\n    \"effort\": \"auto\",\r\n    \"speed\": \"standard\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"status\": \"REVIEW_COMPLETED\",\r\n  \"attempts\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"exitCode\": 0,\r\n      \"provider\": \"claude_cli\",\r\n      \"status\": \"SUCCESS\",\r\n      \"model\": \"claude-opus-5-5\"\r\n    }\r\n  ]\r\n}"
